{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>It is a solemn assembly.</b> The meaning of עצירה (assembly) is not only cessation from ordinary labor, but together with this, a requirement to stand for some time in the holy places, to serve the ever-blessed El there in Torah, in prayer, or in the sacrificial service — as in וְשָׁם אִישׁ מֵעַבְדֵי שָׁאוּל בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא נֶעְצָר לִפְנֵי ה׳ (1 Samuel 21:8), and similarly קַדְּשׁוּ צוֹם קִרְאוּ עֲצָרָה (Joel 1:14), and on this pattern Jehu said קַדְּשׁוּ עֲצָרָה לַבָּעַל (2 Kings 10:20). He said: since this day, after the festival of Sukkot, is the day on which all the festival rejoicings reach their perfection, it is sacred to be a day of assembly in which they assemble in the holy places, and its rejoicing is a rejoicing of Torah and good deeds, as it says: יִשְׂמַח יִשְׂרָאֵל בְּעוֹשָׂיו (Psalms 149:2). This is like וַיְהִי כִּי הִקִּיפוּ יְמֵי הַמִּשְׁתֶּה וַיִּשְׁלַח אִיּוֹב וַיְקַדְּשֵׁם וְהִשְׁכִּים בַּבֹּקֶר וְהֶעֱלָה עוֹלוֹת מִסְפַּר כֻּלָּם, כִּי אָמַר אִיּוֹב אוּלַי חָטְאוּ בָנַי וגו׳ (Job 1:5) — and this was because of the preceding rejoicing. And since on the seventh day of Passover Israel assembled with Moses together to sing to the ever-blessed El, as it says: אָז יָשִׁיר מֹשֶׁה וּבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל (Exodus 15:1), He hallowed that day to be an assembly to YHWH, even though the deliverance did not occur at the start of the day — and this He explained in Mishneh Torah, saying: וּבַיּוֹם הַשְּׁבִיעִי עֲצֶרֶת לַה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ לֹא תַעֲשֶׂה מְלָאכָה (Deuteronomy 16:8). And since the fiftieth day after the Exodus was the day of the giving of the Torah, on which Israel assembled together for the service of the ever-blessed El, our Sages of blessed memory (Moʿed Qatan 6:4) called it Atzeret. However, in the Torah that day is not mentioned by this name at all, because Israel corrupted what was grasped at their assembly: וַיִּתְנַצְּלוּ אֶת עֶדְיָם מֵהַר חוֹרֵב (Exodus 33:6)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The mishnah cited as מועד קטן פרק ו 'אלו מגלחין' corresponds to Moʿed Qatan chapter 3 in standard numbering of the Mishnah; Sforno's chapter reference follows a different arrangement. The phrase 'Mishneh Torah' refers to the book of Deuteronomy, not the Rambam's code."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:45.705669408Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}